  "description": "Demonstrates how to use Java switch statement.  This program determines whether an integer between 1 and 10 is prime. (Prime numbers are integers that are divisible by only themselves and 1.  2 is considered the smallest prime number.)",
  "code": "/*\n * Demonstrates how to use Java switch statement.\n * This program determines whether an integer between 1 and 10 is prime.\n * (Prime numbers are integers that are divisible by only themselves\n *  and 1.  2 is considered the smallest prime number.)\n */\n\npublic class SwitchDemo {\n\tpublic static void main(String[] args) {\n\t\t\n\t\tint x = 13;\n\n\t\tswitch (x) {\n\t\tcase 2:\t\n\t\tcase 3:\n\t\tcase 5:\n\t\tcase 7:\n\t\t\tSystem.out.println(\"Prime\");\n\t\t\tbreak;\n\t\tcase 1:\n\t\tcase 4:\n\t\tcase 6:\n\t\tcase 8:\n\t\tcase 9:\n\t\tcase 10:\n\t\t\tSystem.out.println(\"Not prime\");\n\t\t\tbreak;\n\t\tdefault:\t\n\t\t\tSystem.out.println(\"Sorry, I can handle only numbers between 1 and 10... for now\");\n\t\t}\n\t}\n}\n",
  "line_count": 33,
